module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.hub_cache_root_relative_to_executing_home

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data hub_cache_root_relative_to_executing_home: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "hub_cache_root_relative_to_executing_home" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**the Hugging Face cache root is relative to the executing process's home** (a Hub CLI run inside a --rm container with no HF_HUB_CACHE writes to the container's own ~/.cache/huggingface/hub, so a completed download is deleted with the container while the host cache stays empty).",

    "INVALID STATE: a containerised Hub CLI whose environment does not point HF_HUB_CACHE (or HF_HOME / XDG_CACHE_HOME) at the container side of the mount it was given. The cache path a caller names on the host and the one the CLI resolves are then two different directories.",

    "HARM: 2026-10-03/04 Spark Group A bring-up (valiant-crab-775): each materialize attempt of the GLM snapshot fetched ~300 GB into the container and lost it at exit; the host cache read as never filled and the next attempt started over.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: upstream huggingface_hub constants.py resolves HF_HUB_CACHE > HF_HOME/hub > XDG_CACHE_HOME/huggingface/hub > ~/.cache/huggingface/hub against the EXECUTING process's environment and home (extdeps.huggingface.hub hub_cache_root_for, landed by gunbc#13040). The tell is a host cache directory that stays empty while the CLI reports success.",

    "RUNG: found at 1 (a human noticed the disk). Now 3 for the materialize path: gunbc.spark.model_snapshot_materialize derives the CLI's environment from the mount it declares and refuses (ContainerizedHubCliRefused) when the resolved root is not the mount's container side, so a cache write that would vanish with the container has no constructor there. CEILING 3 overall: every containerised Hub CLI invocation in the corpus routed through that one constructor. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: none for the materialize path; any other Hub CLI invocation site must take its environment from the same constructor, SUFFICIENT FOR no Hub CLI argv in the corpus resolving its cache outside its declared mount. SIBLING, NOT MODELED, BY DECISION: hf 1.33 keeps completed LFS files in a hub-level shared store (<cache_root>/blobs/<2hex>/<sha256>) with each repo's blobs/ holding symlinks into it (read on the Group A hosts 2026-10-04 by valiant-crab-775), so a model directory shrinks as files complete and a mount of the model directory alone hands dangling links. Nothing reads that layout today -- the materialize and launch mounts take the whole cache root -- so modeling it now would be a declaration with no consumer (DESIGN §3c). TRIGGER: a mount narrower than the cache root, or a consumer that resolves blob paths or sizes a model directory, SUFFICIENT FOR that consumer to read the store layout from extdeps.huggingface.hub rather than assume the per-repo blobs/ holds the bytes.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
